{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.PolynomialBarInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.PolynomialBarInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Coeff","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_even_truncated_pre_archimedean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_even_truncated_pre_archimedean","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L372-L380","doc":"**Generic arbitrary-degree even-polynomial truncation is bar-symmetric**\n— over any `CommRing R`. Combines `Arbitrary.barPoly_even_truncated_arbitrary`\nwith the pre-archimedean naming convention. The same theorem, restated\nhere for the §7c discipline: nothing about this requires `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_evenPoly_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_evenPoly_8","kind":"theorem","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L363-L370","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.evenPoly_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.evenPoly_8","kind":"def","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L359-L361","doc":"**Generic degree-8 even-polynomial** in `R[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_evenPoly_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.barPoly_evenPoly_6","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L343-L357","doc":"**Generic `evenPoly_6` is bar-symmetric** over any `CommRing R`,\nno field structure needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.evenPoly_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Generic.evenPoly_6","kind":"def","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L337-L341","doc":"**Generic degree-6 even-polynomial** in `R[X]`:\n$P(X) = c_0 + c_1 X^2 + c_2 X^4 + c_3 X^6$\nfor arbitrary coefficients $c_0, c_1, c_2, c_3 \\in R$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.ArbitraryOdd.barPoly_odd_truncated_arbitrary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.ArbitraryOdd.barPoly_odd_truncated_arbitrary","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L302-L316","doc":"**Arbitrary odd-power truncation is bar-anti-symmetric**:\n\nFor any `c : ℕ → R` and truncation degree `n`,\n$\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} c_k \\, X^{2k+1}$\nis bar-anti-symmetric (bar maps it to its negation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_constant_plus_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_constant_plus_even","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L273-L286","doc":"**Constant-plus-even-truncation is bar-symmetric**: a more\nconvenient form for c_5-like polynomials where the constant\nterm has its own coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_even_finset_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_even_finset_sum","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L260-L271","doc":"**Generic bar-symmetric finite even-power polynomial**:\n`bar (∑ c_k · X^(2k)) = ∑ c_k · X^(2k)` over any Finset index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_even_truncated_arbitrary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.Arbitrary.barPoly_even_truncated_arbitrary","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L233-L258","doc":"**Arbitrary even-power truncation is bar-symmetric**:\n\nFor any natural-number coefficient sequence `c : ℕ → R` and\nany truncation degree `n`, the polynomial\n\n$$P_n(X) \\;=\\; \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} c_k \\, X^{2k}$$\n\nis bar-symmetric.\n\nProof: induction on `n`. Base case: empty sum = 0 is bar-sym.\nInductive step: a new term `c_k · X^(2k)` is bar-sym (constant\nbar-fixed × even-power X bar-fixed), so adding to a bar-sym\nsum preserves bar-symmetry.\n\nThis generalises all three concrete avatar polynomials\n(`c5_taylor_6`, `cos_truncated_6`, `cosh_truncated_6`) to\ntruncations of arbitrary degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.zmod2_X_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.zmod2_X_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L213-L216","doc":"The hypothesis on `2` cannot be dropped: over `ZMod 2`, `X` is bar-fixed\nbut its coefficient of `X¹` is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_fixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_fixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L197-L211","doc":"**Bar-fixed iff odd coefficients vanish**, when `2` is a non-zero-divisor.\nThis is the precise form of \"the bar-symmetric subring is `R[X²]`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.coeff_barPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.coeff_barPoly","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L183-L195","doc":"Coefficients of `bar p`: `(bar p)ₙ = (-1)ⁿ pₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_neg","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L169-L173","doc":"**`bar` distributes over negation**: `bar (-p) = -(bar p)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_sub","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L152-L167","doc":"**`bar` distributes over subtraction**: `bar (p - q) = bar p - bar q`.\nFollows from `bar` being a ring homomorphism (`add` + `bar` of `-1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_c5_denominator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_c5_denominator","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L138-L150","doc":"**`bar (4 + X²) = 4 + X²`** — the polynomial $h^2 + 4$ (the\n`c5` denominator in `c5_as_function_of_skein`) is bar-symmetric.\nConcrete polynomial realisation of \"the c_5 denominator lives\nin the bar-symmetric subring $R[X^2]$\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L127-L136","doc":"**`bar` fixes every natural-number scalar in `R[X]`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_odd","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L118-L125","doc":"**`bar X^(2n+1) = -X^(2n+1)`** — odd powers are bar-anti-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_even","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L108-L116","doc":"**`bar X^(2n) = X^(2n)`** — even powers of the indeterminate\nare bar-symmetric. Concrete polynomial realisation of the\nbar-grading \"anti × anti × ... = sym\" identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L97-L106","doc":"**`bar X^n = (-1)^n · X^n`** — natural-power bar action.\nFollows by induction on `n`: at the inductive step,\n`bar (X^(n+1)) = bar X · bar (X^n) = (-X) · (-1)^n · X^n = (-1)^(n+1) X^(n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X_pow_two","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L91-L95","doc":"**`bar X² = X²`** — the squared indeterminate is bar-symmetric.\nConcrete polynomial realisation of \"anti × anti = sym\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L84-L89","doc":"**`bar` is involutive**: `bar (bar p) = p`.\nProof: substituting `-X` for `X` and then again gives\n`-(-X) = X`, so we recover the identity composition. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:polynomial-bar-involution","label":"prop:polynomial-bar-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L79-L82","doc":"`bar 0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L74-L77","doc":"`bar 1 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_mul","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L69-L72","doc":"`bar` is **multiplicative**: `bar (p · q) = bar p · bar q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_add","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L64-L67","doc":"`bar` is **additive**: `bar (p + q) = bar p + bar q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_C","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L59-L62","doc":"`bar` fixes constants `C c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_neg_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_neg_X","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L54-L57","doc":"`bar (-X) = X`: the involution closes on the indeterminate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly_X","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L49-L52","doc":"`bar X = -X` by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialBarInvolution.barPoly","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/polynomial-bar-involution.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The bar map on `R[X]` sending `X ↦ -X`. Implemented as\n`p.comp (-X)` — substitute `-X` for the indeterminate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}